course: dictionary
lesson: 7348
title: Platinum: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Platinum is a good example. In science it is a metal. In a sentence about hair or music, it means something else entirely. Look at the words around it before you decide.
explain: «Gold, silver and platinum are precious metals.» Here platinum is a noun, the name of a very valuable silvery-white metal. The word «precious» and the list of metals are the clues. A quick check: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «She wore a platinum ring.» Here platinum is an adjective, a describing word. It tells you what the ring is made of. «Her hair was platinum blonde» is different again: it describes a very pale, silver-blonde colour, not a metal at all.
explain: «The band's new song went platinum in a week.» Read the rest of the sentence: a song sold very well, so platinum means a special prize for a huge number of sales. When one word has several meanings, ask yourself which meaning fits the other words in the sentence.
fact: Platinum is a very valuable silvery-white metal. Its chemical symbol is Pt.
fact: Platinum does not rust, and it is heavier than gold.
fact: «Platinum is rarer than gold» and is used in car parts called catalytic converters that clean exhaust fumes.
fact: «Platinum ring» and «platinum blonde» use platinum as an adjective: one means made of platinum, the other means very pale silver-blonde.
fact: A «platinum record» is a prize for an album or song that sells a very great number of copies, and «go platinum» means to reach that level of sales.
exercise: «Gold, silver and platinum are precious metals.» What is platinum in this sentence? | A music prize | A colour of hair | A type of fruit | *A very valuable silvery-white metal
exercise: «She wore a platinum ring on her finger.» What does platinum tell us about the ring? | It is covered in dust | It is made of wood | *It is made of platinum | It is coloured bright red
exercise: «The band's new song went platinum in a week.» What does go platinum mean? | It was made of metal | *It sold a very great number of copies | It was sung very loudly | It was played on the radio once
test: Why is platinum used in car parts that clean exhaust fumes? | Because it turns bright red when hot | Because it is soft and cheap like wood | Because it floats on water | *Because it does not react easily and is rare and valuable
test: Which statement about platinum is true? | It is a type of wood | It is lighter than gold | *It is rarer than gold | It rusts quickly in the rain
exam: Which statement about platinum is true? | *It does not rust and is heavier than gold | It is a sweet fruit | It is a type of wood | It is lighter than gold and rusts easily
